### Uploader share — the write-only drop-box guest surface (uc.sharing.share-uploader, cr-0102, ADR 0031)
# The UPLOADER role reuses the CONTRIBUTOR guest endpoints (name yourself → share-scoped upload) and adds ONE
# new op: delete-your-own — `DELETE /api/shares/{shareId}/media/{mediaId}` with the `contributorToken` in the
# `X-Contributor-Token` header. Like the other guest paths it is genuinely UNAUTHENTICATED (`@PermitAll`),
# gated only by share state + the token. So this asserts REAL guest behavior — a well-formed but unknown share
# is a non-enumerable 404 (`share_media_not_found`, NOT a 401), which proves the delete path is public and does
# not enumerate.
#
# The full behavior — an UPLOADER resolve serves `media: []` even with existing media (write-only), an uploader
# names itself + uploads (attaches to the shared root, stamped with the identity), delete-own reclaims the
# media + its blobs on a single-row ownership check, and a foreign-identity / bad-token / VIEWER-share delete is
# rejected (404 / 403) — is covered hermetically at the integration layer (ShareUploaderSliceTest, which seeds a
# member + personal scope + a Memory in-tx) and end-to-end in the web client's live smoke. Those need the
# operator-blind grant flow + client-side crypto, not a bare .http.
#
# Run: ijhttp --env-file http/sharing/http-client.env.json --env dev http/sharing/uploader.http

### 1. Delete-own on a well-formed but unknown share (well-formed token) → 404 (public + non-enumerable)
DELETE {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA/media/7c3f0e2a-9b1d-4a6e-8b2c-1f2d3e4a5b6c
X-Contributor-Token: bm90LXJlYWwtdG9rZW4tYnV0LXdlbGwtZm9ybWVkLTE

> {%
client.test("delete-own on an unknown share is a public, non-enumerable 404", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 404, "expected 404, got " + response.status);
    client.assert(response.body.code === "share_media_not_found", "expected share_media_not_found");
});
%}

### 2. Delete-own with a malformed token (not 43-char base64url) → 400 at the boundary (bean-validation, before the handler)
DELETE {{host}}/api/shares/AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA/media/7c3f0e2a-9b1d-4a6e-8b2c-1f2d3e4a5b6c
X-Contributor-Token: too-short

> {%
client.test("a malformed contributor token is rejected at the boundary (400)", function () {
    client.assert(response.status === 400, "expected 400, got " + response.status);
});
%}
